  "cause_evidence": [
    "The original rate-limited test carrier uses TransportTypeUnknown gateways; H1 service sampling, pending physical tails and controlled drains remain inactive.",
    "The carrier serializes one frame, waits on its timer, then resets the following departure to current wall time. Late wakes become extra per-frame service time even with queued input.",
    "Under the real-clock diagnostic, the pump lost472-758ms per3s arm, almost entirely while its input remained queued. Diagnostic polling occurred only after measurement.",
    "A virtual-time100us delayed wake forced only in the delivery arm reproduces the original relative assertion deterministically3/3 with identical production code and configured capacity.",
    "The proposed test runs both actual clients and the same carrier in virtual time, retains the90% relative gate and peer-capacity clamp, and additionally requires each arm to deliver90%-101% of configured carrier byte rate, sampled window activation and no expired accepted frames."
  ],
